116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 41 0 R
/T (This report presents the implementation and deployment of a smart sensor and lighting control unit using the Espressif ESP32 microcontroller. Built inside the PlatformIO IDE framework on VS Code, the system integrates an Infrared \(IR\) proximity sensor and a potentiometer to execute layered digital and analog tracking. The system uses an interlocking logic architecture: an active indicator LED is kept entirely off by default, turning on only when the digital IR sensor detects a nearby object. Once active, its real-time brightness is dynamically adjusted from 0% to 100% using hardware-driven Pulse Width Modulation \(PWM\) tied directly to the analog position of the potentiometer knob. System diagnostics, including raw sensor counts, calculated input voltage, and actual LED intensity, are piped continuously via an asynchronous UART connection to a monitoring workstation at 115200 baud. All project deliverables have been successfully modularized and pushed into the centralized monorepo structure on GitHub, with collaborator permissions granted for technical evaluation.)
/E (This report presents the implementation and deployment of a smart sensor and lighting control unit using the Espressif ESP32 microcontroller. Built inside the PlatformIO IDE framework on VS Code, the system integrates an Infrared \(IR\) proximity sensor and a potentiometer to execute layered digital and analog tracking. The system uses an interlocking logic architecture: an active indicator LED is kept entirely off by default, turning on only when the digital IR sensor detects a nearby object. Once active, its real-time brightness is dynamically adjusted from 0% to 100% using hardware-driven Pulse Width Modulation \(PWM\) tied directly to the analog position of the potentiometer knob. System diagnostics, including raw sensor counts, calculated input voltage, and actual LED intensity, are piped continuously via an asynchronous UART connection to a monitoring workstation at 115200 baud. All project deliverables have been successfully modularized and pushed into the centralized monorepo structure on GitHub, with collaborator permissions granted for technical evaluation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [40]
>>
endobj
