<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 695 0 R
/T (System Gating: The system treats the digital IR sensor input as an operational master gate. The ESP32 constantly polls the status of the IR sensor and the voltage level of the potentiometer wiper.)
/E (System Gating: The system treats the digital IR sensor input as an operational master gate. The ESP32 constantly polls the status of the IR sensor and the voltage level of the potentiometer wiper.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
222 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 696 0 R
/T <>
/E <>
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 697 0 R
/T (Inactive State Interlock: When the IR sensor reads HIGH \(Target Inactive\), the firmware overrides all potentiometer positions, setting the PWM output registers directly to 0. This ensures total firmware control over peripheral states based on priority input gates.)
/E (Inactive State Interlock: When the IR sensor reads HIGH \(Target Inactive\), the firmware overrides all potentiometer positions, setting the PWM output registers directly to 0. This ensures total firmware control over peripheral states based on priority input gates.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
